  "after_installed_descriptions": {
    "agent-zero": "Use when starting an Agent Zero session or deciding how to turn Shaan's request into checked, landed work across existing owners.",
    "a0-dispatch": "Use when sending a bounded job to an existing Agent Zero owner or seat; records the dispatch and arms the completion waiter.",
    "job-brief": "Use when compiling a request into a builder job with quoted intent, owned files, constraints and one executable acceptance check.",
    "shaan-report": "Use when returning a deliverable to Shaan; lead with his next action, then verified changes, evidence and remaining limits.",
    "research-fleet": "Use when a research question needs independent slices and one evidence-backed synthesis from an Agent Zero fleet.",
    "deletion-pass": "Use when simplifying a system or retiring duplicate code, skills, tests or jobs; inspect consumers, preserve an archive and verify the remaining path.",
    "haiku-team": "Use when research, audits, maps or independent build jobs need a Haiku team or parallel builders; split bounded slices and integrate one checked return.",
    "look": "Use when Agent Zero needs current queue and seat status or must wait for dispatched work; wraps look, a0-await and waitfor without manual polling.",
    "librarian": "Use when finding an existing repo, tool, skill, prior decision or research before building; search recall and estate where, then return exact source paths.",
    "codex-run": "Use when dispatching an implementation job or coordinating parallel builders with disjoint files; resolve routing, run codex-run and integrate checked artifacts.",
    "land": "Use when landing checked work in sisodias/siso or diagnosing a red or missing siso-ci status; run the repository land command and preserve guard failures.",
    "show-page": "Use when showing Shaan a page, screenshot comparison or UI result; inspect the artifact, then return a real show-page URL or supported inline screenshot view.",
    "self-compact": "Use when context is filling, a compaction ping arrives or Shaan requests a checkpoint; save state and arm self-compact at a clean break. Agent Zero follows its own compaction rule.",
    "a0-upgrade": "Use when shipping one filed Agent Zero improvement; start its isolated upgrade worktree, run one meaningful check and ship with a0-upgrade.",
    "skill-author": "Use when any agent adds, edits, registers or installs a skill; reuse the Hub source, write trigger cases first, validate and verify the installed files.",
    "siso-ui": "Use when building or restyling a SISO screen or component; start with the surface standard and Shaan's curated UI picks, then inspect rendered results.",
    "camofox": "Use when reading, navigating or taking screenshots of a web page headlessly through the local Camofox REST API without opening a browser on Shaan's screen.",
    "machine-reach": "Use when connecting to the Mac mini or a SISO VPS, or diagnosing SSH reachability; resolve the current alias and try documented routes in order.",
    "fleet-check": "Use when asking what agents are doing, which seat is stuck or why a run stopped; run fleet-check for current evidence before reading transcripts.",
    "token-ledger": "Use when asking where Claude tokens or spend went by seat, model, login or time window; run token-ledger and report measured totals and coverage."
